Automatic note creation and Claude Stop consume one bounded commit classifier: a nonempty commit changing only .span, .spans, or the configured span root is metadata-only; mixed commits remain material. The writer acknowledges metadata-only receipts without a notes association, while Claude Stop also ignores such pre-existing or manually added notes and advances its observed-ID checkpoint. Empty commits retain writer notes but do not request Claude review. Classifier lookup failures retain receipts and do not advance the Stop checkpoint. Merge-parent paths and rename source/destination paths participate in classification, so moving metadata into source remains material; the current writer regression checks default-root metadata receipts for Claude and Codex, while the Stop tests cover configured roots and mixed commits.
